这也是你能评估的部分。

55
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:58,150
And then you can address this
然后你可以通过采取相应的控制措施

56
00:02:58,150 --> 00:03:00,090
by applying the pertinent controls.
来应对它。

57
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:02,210
However, there are risks that are beyond
不过，也有一些风险超出了

58
00:03:02,210 --> 00:03:03,790
the scope of the assessment.
评估的范围。

59
00:03:03,790 --> 00:03:05,550
And this is what you do not see.
这是你看不到的部分。

60
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:08,270
For instance, if you are working
例如，如果你处理的是

61
00:03:08,270 --> 00:03:12,410
with a risk group to biological agent,
危险度2级的生物因子，

62
00:03:12,410 --> 00:03:16,650
and one of your laboratory workers has an allergy,
而你的一位实验室工作人员有过敏症，

63
00:03:16,650 --> 00:03:19,490
which he or she has not reported earlier
他或她之前没有报告过，

64
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:21,090
because they were not aware of it,
因为他们自己也不知道，

65
00:03:21,090 --> 00:03:24,530
exposure to this RG2 biological agent
那么接触这种RG2生物因子

66
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:28,450
can cause morbidity or even mortality.
可能导致发病甚至死亡。

67
00:03:28,450 --> 00:03:31,610
So these are risks which you must anticipate,
所以这些风险你必须有所预料，

68
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:33,930
but they are what are known as unknown risks
但它们属于所谓的未知风险，

69
00:03:33,930 --> 00:03:42,150
that are beyond the scope of assessment.
超出了评估的范围。

70
00:03:42,150 --> 00:03:45,150
We will now look at microbiological risk assessment
下面我们来看基于世卫组织《实验室生物安全手册》的

71
00:03:45,150 --> 00:03:48,310
based on the WHO laboratory biosafety manual
微生物风险评估，

72
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:49,950
and discuss the development
并讨论风险评估工具的

73
00:03:49,950 --> 00:03:54,710
of an instrument for risk assessment.
制定。

74
00:03:54,710 --> 00:03:57,750
These are some of the factors which you must consider
以下是你在开展风险评估时

75
00:03:57,750 --> 00:04:00,430
when you conduct a risk assessment.
必须考虑的一些因素。

76
00:04:00,430 --> 00:04:02,190
The first one is the pathogenicity
第一个是生物因子的

77
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:05,350
of the biological agent and the infectious dose.
致病性和感染剂量。

78
00:04:06,950 --> 00:04:09,510
Is the microorganism a pathogen
这种微生物是否是已有报道会造成

79
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:13,610
which has been reported to cause mortality and mobility?
死亡和发病的病原体？

80
00:04:13,610 --> 00:04:15,610
And what is the infectious dose?
感染剂量是多少？

81
00:04:15,610 --> 00:04:18,490
How many colony forming units
这种微生物需要多少个菌落形成单位

82
00:04:18,490 --> 00:04:23,490
or particles of this particular microorganism
或多少个颗粒

83
00:04:23,770 --> 00:04:28,170
are sufficient in order to cause infection?
才足以引起感染？

84
00:04:28,170 --> 00:04:31,330
And this varies from individual to individual,
这因人而异，

85
00:04:31,330 --> 00:04:35,190
from environmental condition to environmental condition,
也因环境条件而异，

86
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:36,990
but you must assess this risk
但你必须从致病性和感染剂量的角度

87
00:04:36,990 --> 00:04:40,650
in terms of the pathogenicity and infectious dose.
评估这一风险。

88
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:44,090
The second aspect is the potential outcome of exposure.
第二个方面是暴露的可能后果。

89
00:04:44,090 --> 00:04:48,070
Does it result in morbidity, mortality?
它会导致发病还是死亡？

90
00:04:48,070 --> 00:04:51,350
What is the natural route of infection?
自然感染途径是什么？

91
00:04:51,350 --> 00:04:53,990
Is it via the nasal passages?
是通过鼻腔吗？

92
00:04:53,990 --> 00:04:56,290
Is it through the skin?
是通过皮肤吗？

93
00:04:56,290 --> 00:04:58,430
Or is it subdermal below the skin?
还是经皮下、皮肤以下？

94
00:04:58,430 --> 00:04:59,950
Or is it via ingestion?
或者是通过食入？

95
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:02,030
What is the route of infection?
感染途径是什么？

96
00:05:02,030 --> 00:05:03,870
What are the other routes of infection?
还有哪些其他感染途径？

97
00:05:03,870 --> 00:05:06,010
Does it have multiple routes of infection?
它是否有多种感染途径？

98
00:05:06,990 --> 00:05:10,770
And are these the result of laboratory manipulation?
这些途径是否是实验室操作造成的？

99
00:05:10,770 --> 00:05:15,770
So for instance, if you are culturing a lab pathogen,
例如，如果你在培养实验室病原体，

100
00:05:17,830 --> 00:05:20,670
basically cultivating a pathogen
也就是在实验室里

101
00:05:20,670 --> 00:05:22,790
in the laboratory using enriched media,
用富集培养基培养病原体，

102
00:05:22,790 --> 00:05:26,810
if there is a spill in the lab with the enriched media,
如果实验室里发生了富集培养基的溢洒，

103
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:31,810
this particular pathogen is more likely to cause harm
这种病原体就更有可能

104
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:33,030
to the laboratory workers
对实验室工作人员造成危害，

105
00:05:33,030 --> 00:05:37,030
because you have increased the culture volume
因为你增加了培养体积，

106
00:05:37,030 --> 00:05:40,110
and this represents laboratory manipulation.
而这就属于实验室操作。

107
00:05:40,110 --> 00:05:42,390
Then we look at the stability of the biological agent
然后我们看生物因子在环境中的

108
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:43,230
in the environment.
稳定性。

109
00:05:43,230 --> 00:05:45,110
For instance, in the case of coronavirus,
例如，就冠状病毒而言，

110
00:05:45,110 --> 00:05:48,550
there have been multiple reports of stability studies
已有多项稳定性研究报告称，

111
00:05:48,550 --> 00:05:52,590
reporting that the virus may be stable for longer
该病毒保持稳定的时间

112
00:05:52,590 --> 00:05:56,990
than other viruses for a longer duration of time
可能比其他病毒更长，

113
00:05:56,990 --> 00:05:58,290
in the environment.
在环境中就是这样。

114
00:05:58,290 --> 00:06:01,070
Then we look at the concentration and culture volume
接着我们看生物因子的浓度

115
00:06:01,070 --> 00:06:02,610
of the biological agent.
和培养体积。

116
00:06:02,610 --> 00:06:04,910
Now, as a general principle,
作为一般原则，

117
00:06:04,910 --> 00:06:07,610
when working with pathogens in the laboratory,
在实验室中处理病原体时，

118
00:06:08,530 --> 00:06:12,250
we must minimize this culture volume
我们必须把培养体积降到最低，

119
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:14,770
because a very high culture volume can lead
因为培养体积过大可能导致

120
00:06:14,770 --> 00:06:19,770
to potential spills and the consequent infections.
溢洒以及由此引发的感染。

121
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:27,280
We also look at the presence of a suitable host.
我们还要看是否存在适宜的宿主。

122
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:31,000
For instance, if you are cultivating a parasite
例如，如果你在实验室中

123
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,020
in the laboratory,
培养某种寄生虫，

124
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:35,040
if there is no mosquito over the vector
如果没有蚊子这类媒介

125
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:39,840
to transmit this parasite from the animal into the human,
把这种寄生虫从动物传给人，

126
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:43,440
the likelihood of infection and transmission
那么感染和传播的可能性

127
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:45,320
is very, very low.
就非常非常低。

128
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:47,620
We also look at a priori information,
我们还要看先验信息，

129
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,440
which is available from research papers
这些信息可以从研究论文、

130
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:54,080
and clinical reports and epidemiological studies.
临床报告和流行病学研究中获得。

131
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,840
We look at the laboratory procedures during risk assessment.
在风险评估中我们要看实验室操作程序。

132
00:06:56,840 --> 00:07:00,000
Does it involve centrifugation, aerosolization
是否涉及离心、用移液器

133
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,560
of the content using pipettes
使内容物形成气溶胶，

134
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,360
or does it involve any other procedures
或者是否涉及其他操作程序，

135
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:06,940
such as microscopy,
比如显微镜检查，

136
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:10,560
which can pose a risk to the laboratory user.
这些都可能给实验室使用者带来风险。

137
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:13,640
Any genetic manipulation has the microbe
任何基因操作，该微生物

138
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:16,880
or the biological agent being genetically modified.
或生物因子是否经过基因改造。

139
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:21,200
And we look at local availability of effective profile axis,
我们还要看当地能否获得有效的预防性措施，

140
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:22,860
which is preventive treatment,
也就是预防性治疗，

141
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:29,800
or therapeutic interventions for this particular pathogen.
或针对该病原体的治疗干预措施。

142
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:32,040
This is a risk instrument.
这是一份风险评估工具。

143
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,360
It's an example,
这只是一个示例，

144
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:36,240
and you may have to adapt this for your own laboratory
你可能需要针对自己实验室的

145
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
for your virus management scenario.
生物风险管理情形加以调整。

146
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:42,120
The first question is,
第一个问题是：

147
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:46,960
has the biological agent been reported to be a pathogen?
该生物因子是否已有报道是病原体？

148
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:50,280
So if newly emerging pathogens
新出现的病原体

149
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:54,120
may not have been reported earlier,
可能此前没有报道，

150
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:56,800
and this may lead to lack of alertness
这可能导致生物风险管理者

151
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:59,560
on the part of the virus managers.
缺乏警觉。

152
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:03,940
So every biological agent must be treated with caution
因此，对每一种生物因子都必须谨慎对待，

153
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:05,600
based on earlier reports
既要依据以往的报道，

154
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:08,240
as well as currently developing situations.
也要考虑当前的发展形势。

155
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:13,640
Does exposure to the biological agent lead to morbidity?
接触该生物因子是否会导致发病？

156
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:17,360
So you have, so if this is yes, and this is yes,
如果这项是“是”，这项也是“是”，

157
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:20,160
so morbidity means your laboratory workers
发病意味着你的实验室工作人员

158
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:23,480
are likely to get sick if they're exposed
一旦暴露就可能生病，

159
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:26,440
and may have to be hospitalized.
而且可能需要住院。

160
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:30,280
Is the root of infection via inhalation?
感染途径是否经由吸入？

161
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:32,720
If yes, then you click yes.
如果是，就勾选“是”。

162
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:36,320
Is the root of infection via contact?
感染途径是否经由接触？

163
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:38,000
No, then you click no.
如果不是，就勾选“否”。

164
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:41,840
Is the biological agent stable in the environment?
该生物因子在环境中是否稳定？

165
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:43,240
Of course, if you pose this question,
当然，如果你提出这个问题，

166
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,760
you have to pose other questions such as if yes,
就还要提出其他问题，比如如果稳定，

167
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:48,680
then how long, how many seconds?
那么能维持多久，多少秒？

168
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:51,680
And is it viable on surfaces?
它在物体表面是否存活？

169
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:57,400
Or is it viable in the air at that local temperature?
在当地温度下它在空气中是否存活？

170
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:00,120
Has the biological agent been genetically modified?
该生物因子是否经过基因改造？

171
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:03,960
This can be obtained by our genome sequencing reports.
这可以从基因组测序报告中获知。

172
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,880
And is the treatment readily available?
治疗是否容易获得？

173
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:09,580
These are some of the key questions
这些就是你在制定

174
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:12,120
which you must address when you develop
风险评估工具时

175
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:14,700
instrument for risk assessment.
必须解决的一些关键问题。

176
